From 687469b527f0e224518bcb6e7eaeb584a3566a79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:15:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): share draft placement with first-send workspace
 resolution [daveey]

Replace per-writer draft cwd mirrors with one pure resolver and reactive main-draft cwd used by both sidebar and session creation. Default seeding, normalized local/owned project targets, folder picks and Home detachment now use identical intent. Preserve main's fallback only at the center-tile ambient-workspace boundary, including focus returning to main.

Use the captured create cwd when the create response omits cwd, rather than letting the optimistic Home row inherit an unrelated ambient project.

Proof: eight invariant regressions fail on the prior head (six draft placement mismatches and two detached optimistic placement mismatches). The tile-return invariant fails when the tile boundary capture is reverted. Focused 26 tests and full Desktop typecheck pass; expanded sidebar gate also exercised before the final tile control. Fresh exact-head CI and independent review required.
